1
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:09,750
Brother against brother, father against son. All
competing for...THE COOLANGATTA GOLD!

2
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:13,500
The Coolangatta Gold is a drama film directed by Igor Auzins.

3
00:21:11,250 --> 00:21:17,250
Steve Lucas is a nineteen year old who is filled with the burning
resentment of being forced to live in his brother's shadow.

4
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:21,000
His brother Adam, is burdened by his father's desire for glory, and must win The Coolangatta Gold Tri-Aquathon, It is the greatest endurance test of them all: a marathon involving
a 20 kilometer beach run, 6 kilometer swim and a 17 kilometer surf ski from Surfers Paradise along the golden arc of beach to Coolangatta and back to the start.

5
00:35:18,750 --> 00:35:24,750
The Coolangatta Gold is a story of human endeavor and
endurance against overwhelming odds.

6
00:42:22,500 --> 00:42:28,500
Steve Lucas, played by Joss McWilliam.

7
00:49:26,250 --> 00:49:32,250
Adam Lucas, played by Colin Friels.

8
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:36,000
Joe Lucas, played by Nick Tate.

9
01:03:33,750 --> 01:03:39,750
Kerri Dean, played by Josephine Smulders.

10
01:10:37,500 --> 01:10:43,500
Robyn Lucas, played by Robyn Nevin.

11
01:17:41,250 --> 01:17:47,250
Grant, played by Grant Kenny.

12
01:24:45,000 --> 01:24:51,000
The Coolangatta Gold is a 1984 Australian film directed by Igor
Auzins and written by Peter Schreck and Ted Robinson.

13
01:31:48,750 --> 01:31:54,750
It led to the establishment of the iron man race The Coolangatta
Gold in Coolangatta, on the Gold Coast, Queensland.

14
01:38:52,500 --> 01:38:58,500
The film explores themes of underdog, obsession,
plantation, training, motorcycle crash.

15
01:45:56,250 --> 01:46:02,250
The tone is emotional.
